<!DOCTYPE html>
<!-- Quantum HTML + CSS example 09_backgrounds_gradients/16: Frosted glass -->
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="utf-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
  <title>Frosted glass</title>
  <style>
    *, *::before, *::after { box-sizing: border-box; }
    body {
      margin: 0;
      font-family: system-ui, -apple-system, "Segoe UI", Roboto, sans-serif;
      line-height: 1.5;
      color: #1f2933;
      background: #f5f7fa;
    }
    .demo { max-width: 60rem; margin: 0 auto; padding: 2rem 1.25rem; }
    .demo > h1 { margin: 0 0 0.25rem; font-size: 2rem; }
    .lead { margin: 0 0 2rem; color: #52606d; }

    .scene { padding: 3rem; border-radius: 20px; background: radial-gradient(circle at 20% 20%, #f472b6, transparent 40%), radial-gradient(circle at 80% 70%, #38bdf8, transparent 40%), #312e81; }
    .glass { max-width: 22rem; padding: 2rem; border-radius: 16px; color: #fff; background: rgb(255 255 255 / 0.15); border: 1px solid rgb(255 255 255 / 0.3); backdrop-filter: blur(14px) saturate(140%); }
  </style>
</head>
<body>
  <main class="demo">
    <h1>Frosted glass</h1>
    <p class="lead">backdrop-filter blurs whatever is behind a panel.</p>
    <div class="scene"><div class="glass"><h2>Glass card</h2><p>The colourful shapes behind are blurred by backdrop-filter.</p></div></div>
  </main>
</body>
</html>
